      "evidence": "[F2] states smooth base-change and composition stability only for globally smooth morphisms, plus pointwise relative-dimension additivity. Proof 1.1 invokes it when f is smooth only at x; Proof 2.2 and pointwise clause 3.1 similarly infer smoothness of a composite from pointwise hypotheses. The dimension formula alone does not establish smoothness, which étaleness also requires. The pointwise stability consequence must be supplied or cited; Stacks 29.37.3–.4 supports the global clauses.",
